.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pgloupe-doctor 1  "doctor " 
.SH NAME
pgloupe\-doctor \- Check what the server and the role lack for a useful report, and how to fix it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpgloupe doctor\fR [\fB\-\-password\-env\fR] [\fB\-\-sslrootcert\fR] [\fB\-\-vendor\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-conn\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check what the server and the role lack for a useful report, and how to fix it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-conn\fR \fI<CONN>\fR
Connection string: `postgres://user@host:5432/db` or `key=value` pairs. The password comes from the string, `PGPASSWORD` (or `\-\-password\-env`), or `~/.pgpass`; prefer those to putting it on the command line
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-env\fR \fI<PASSWORD_ENV>\fR
Environment variable that holds the password (default `PGPASSWORD`)
.TP
\fB\-\-sslrootcert\fR \fI<SSLROOTCERT>\fR
CA certificate (PEM) to trust; turns on full certificate and host name checking. For RDS, the regional bundle from AWS
.TP
\fB\-\-vendor\fR \fI<VENDOR>\fR
Say where settings live for this vendor
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
rds: Amazon RDS and Aurora PostgreSQL: settings live in the parameter group
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: text]
Output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: Human\-readable
.IP \(bu 2
json: One JSON document
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
